# Bounded reads

A list paints with one page. The next page and the search box ask the server for more. Do not load every row and slice it in the browser.

The default page size is `LIST_PAGE_SIZE` (25) from `@hrms/db/page`. The table can switch to 25, 50, 100, or 200. `pageSizeOf` rejects any other size. A list result is `{ rows, totalCount, page, pageSize }`. `totalCount` is `COUNT(*) OVER()` on the same statement. `pageOf` clamps the page to `1..10000`. Offset is `(page - 1) * pageSize`. Changing the size returns to page 1.

Empty search returns page 1 of the ordered set. `searchText` ignores fewer than 2 characters. A real search is a `LIKE` (or the screen's existing filters) and resets to page 1.

The screen owns `?page=`, `?pageSize=`, and `?q=`. Omit `page` when it is 1, omit `pageSize` when it is 25, and omit `q` when it is empty. `DataTable` is server-paged when `pagination.current` and `pagination.total` are set and `onSearch` is passed. That search box calls `onSearch`. It does not hide rows that are already the server's page.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — every employee, then the table pages in memory
const hits = await searchEmployees(db, employerId, "");

// ✅ GOOD — one page, and a short search is ignored
const page = pageQuery(filters.page);
const q = searchText(filters.q);
```

```sql
ORDER BY Employee.EmployeeId ASC
OFFSET @offset ROWS FETCH NEXT 25 ROWS ONLY
```

Azure DevOps is not SQL. Load a working set (one sprint, the first 50 commits, recent paths). Search calls Azure. Do not walk a whole repo file tree, every project member, or every area path on first paint.

Leave these alone:

- One-record reads (one employee, one workflow, one upload header, one change request).
- Tools that already cap with `TOP`: Data Builder Studio select, data-fix browse, value search.
